 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Logical-time work queue. All method times are non-decreasing across calls. Before handling any call at time t, every reservation with reservedAt+leaseDuration <= t expires, processed in (deadline, reservation order). A task released by expiry or by fail() returns to the tail of the ready queue if its reservation count is below maxAttempts, otherwise it is moved to the dead-letter queue (DLQ). reserve(t) pops the ready head, counts an attempt and returns its id, or -1. complete(t,id) / fail(t,id) return true iff id currently holds an unexpired reservation; complete finishes it permanently. getDeadLetters(t) returns DLQ ids in the order they entered it. Concurrency is modelled as this deterministic single-threaded call sequence. Level 2 (GRAPH tag): dependencies [before, after] form a DAG; a task is ready initially only without prerequisites, and joins the ready tail when its last prerequisite completes (several unlocked at once join in taskIds order). When a task is dead-lettered, every not-yet-dead transitive dependent is dead-lettered too, breadth-first, each node's dependents in taskIds order.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk02-d-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
